# Intent: The filler pack reader inflates with the K10 helper (its deflated index.json used the ROM call that keeps 11 KB of state on the caller's stack; no filler pack had been pushed to a real unit before this work). The loader gives language packs and phrase packs to their users (K11, K12): has_user covers look, filler, language and phrase; apply and remove call maipai_lang_load_pack and maipai_phrasepack_load; the boot task applies a cached language or phrase pack once the face is up, like the look and the filler pack, and falls back to English and to the image's clips when the cache is empty or damaged. self.pack.status adds lang (the code in use) for the language type and clips (how many of the sixteen came from the pack) for the phrase type, and the boot line names all four types. The sound and dance types stay in the loader and the cache with no consumer (see docs/design/packs-fillers-languages-2026-11-17.md).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_packs.cc and maipai_filler.cc (ours, TB02, TB03, TC03, FM04)
# Check after a flash: self.pack.status for language, phrase, look and filler; send a language pack and read lang; send a phrase pack and read clips 16; flip a bit in the cache (bench) and the status says damaged and the words are English and the clips are the image's; remove each type and the status says fallback true.

